Experiment 3(a)
Title: To execute commands using command separators (;), pipes (|), and output redirection (>) in Linux.

Steps / Commands Executed:
date; w | cat > who.txt

date; — Executes the date command to display the current system date and time directly on the screen.  
w | cat > who.txt — Runs the w command (showing who is logged in and what they are doing), pipes (|) the output into cat, and redirects (>) the final output to save it inside who.txt.

Verify/View the contents of the created file:
cat who.txt
